  "answer": "Under the Manual’s search-indexing practice (not legislation):\n\n- **Letters generally:** use the constituent `LTR` to indicate a letter or letters. [TMM/Part5/x-word-constituents/letters]\n- **Single letters:** add `#` to the constituents as well as `LTR`. [TMM/Part5/x-word-constituents/letters]\n- **Letter groups:** add an additional constituent prefixed with `=`. This distinguishes a group of letters from the same letters used as a word. [TMM/Part5/x-word-constituents/letters]\n- **Acronyms:** where a group is clearly an acronym, index it as letters even if it spells a word. [TMM/Part5/x-word-constituents/letters]"
